# Develop {{project_name}}

Parent: [Documentation index](README.md)

Python 3.11 or newer runs all repository tooling. PowerShell and POSIX shell
files are only platform entrypoints into Python.

## Set up

Run `scripts/setup.ps1` from PowerShell or `scripts/setup.sh` from a POSIX shell.
The workspace runner reads `workspace.toml` and sets up each component in its
declared order.

## Run checks

Run `scripts/check.ps1` from PowerShell or `scripts/check.sh` from a POSIX shell.
The command validates the repository once, then runs every component's runtime
checks.

{{local_ci_docs}}

## Tool ownership

`scripts/workspace.py` owns workspace orchestration. Each component's
`scripts/dev.py` owns only its runtime-specific setup and checks.
